    "title": "Jung Hoo Lee Detained Briefly at LAX Due to Paperwork Issue",
    "text": "• San Francisco Giants outfielder Jung Hoo Lee was briefly detained at Los Angeles International Airport (LAX) on Wednesday.\n• Lee's detention was due to missing paperwork.\n• Lee was arriving from Korea.\n• The Giants stated the issue was quickly clarified with authorities.\n• Lee has been cleared to continue his travel.\n• Lee signed a six-year, $113 million contract with the Giants in December 2023.\n• Lee missed most of his rookie season in 2024 due to a dislocated left shoulder.\n• In the past year, Lee batted .266 with eight home runs, 55 RBIs, and 10 stolen bases over 150 games.\n• Lee started 144 games in center field.",
